    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d579">

                <pb facs="0552" n="544" sameAs="frus:frus1940v04/pg544"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.516/693: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Grew</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-10-24T14:00:00-05:00">October 24, 1940—2
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>418. Reference your 1027, October 22, 5 p.m. The Department concurs in your
                    suggested course of action. It is assumed, of course, that in your communication
                    to the Minister for Foreign Affairs you will not use the term “Chinese
                    Government at Nanking”.<anchor n="27" xml:id="d579-f1"/></p>
                <p>Sent to Tokyo via Shanghai. Repeated to Peiping, Nanking.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d579-f1" n="27" xml:id="d579-f1-content">
                <p>In telegram No. 1058, October 26, 7 p.m., the Ambassador in Japan reported that
                    representations were made to the Japanese Foreign Minister on that date
                    (893.516/698).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
